depends search
# these two queries shouldn't need to access the bodyparts table
# at all. this isn't tested here, but the searches need to be
# somewhere... the only way I know of testing is 'explain analyze'.
#
# the FROM bit is true for all messages, so pg should be able to
# short-circuit OR and not test BODY at all. and a seqscan should
# definitely not be needed.
send 1
1533 uid SEARCH UNDELETED (OR FROM "arnt" BODY "word")
receive 2
* SEARCH 1 2 3 4 5 6
1533 OK done
# there are no deleted messages, so neither FROM now BODY should need
# evaluation. the planner may plan, but most of the plan should never be
# executed.
send 1
1533 uid SEARCH DELETED FROM "arnt" BODY "word"
receive 2
* SEARCH
1533 OK done
end
